I am sitting in the S-Bahn.
I am going home.
The train is not very full.
I have a seat by the window.
I look out of the window.
I see the streets and buildings.
The train goes straight ahead through the city.
I see the city map in my head again.
I am travelling from Museum Island to my flat.
I know the way much better now.
At my station I get off.
There I first go to the left.
Then I keep going straight ahead.
And then I turn right.
I see my part of Berlin very exactly.
I know my neighbourhood now.
The big city is not so unfamiliar anymore.
That is a really nice feeling.
Tomorrow I might ride my bicycle through the streets.
But now I am simply tired.
